# Adraodan Minotaur

## Lore

The Adraodan are one of three Minotaur tribes that sealed themselves beneath what is now the Sandy Desert some seventy thousand years ago, ashamed of their ancestors'' service to the Old Ones. Where their neighbours sank into despair or slid back into evil, the Adraodan kept their vow. They gave up dark gods and sorcery for good, prayed for forgiveness, and built a culture around compassion and service. Over the ages that devotion changed them: every member of the tribe is now a psychic of some kind.

When an Earthshaker broke open their caverns, the Adraodan took it as the sign they had waited for. They mean to walk out into a world they know nothing about - they have never heard of humans, and expect to find the old empires of Elves, Dwarves and Titans - and prove that a Minotaur can be a hero. Their plan is to split into four parties, travel to the four corners of the world, and then scatter into small bands and lone wanderers who fight evil wherever they meet it.

Their first battle has already been fought, against the Kkairojan tribe, who came out of the same caverns sworn to the Old Ones. Most Adraodan feel bound to hunt the Kkairojan down, whatever it costs.

**Alignment:** Any, but most are good or unprincipled; anarchist and evil Adraodan are rare.

**Physical Appearance:** Horned and bull-headed like any Minotaur and powerfully built, but of a lighter frame than their surface kin, the mark of ages spent below ground. They are pale, anywhere from whitish to light grey, with dark hair and yellow-green eyes.

**Height:** About 7.6 to 9 feet (2.3 to 2.7 m). **Weight:** 400 to 650 pounds (180 to 292 kg).

**Average Life Span:** 400 years; few pass 500.

**Habitat:** Anywhere they can reach in time, but for years to come mostly in and around the Baalgor Wastelands, the Old Kingdom and the Eastern Territory.

**Enemies:** Evil in all its forms, and the Kkairojan Minotaurs above all. **Allies:** Anyone who serves good.

**Favorite Weapons:** None yet.

## GM Notes

There are 2,724 Adraodan. The cave-in killed 423 and the fight with the Kkairojan another 91. The desert crossing should cost them no more than 10-15% of their number, far fewer than the Eirokan tribe would lose.

They are idealists with no experience of the surface: honest, eager and easy to mislead. Whoever they meet first will shape what they become, and the player characters may be those people. Play up what they do not know - humans, the fall of the Elven and Dwarven empires, the Great War - as much as what they can do.

A Minotaur''s horn has a market among alchemists, at as much as 1500 gold, but it is hard to tell from an ordinary bull''s and buyers suspect forgery.

The tribe''s leader was Nekaradon, a principled 3rd level Crusader of Light, 92 years old, who intends to see her people out of the Wastelands and then travel north alone.
